## Why This Is Asked
Tests memory ownership across Go and C, preallocated buffers, and error translation. Avoids Go allocations inside C paths and checks thread-safety under concurrency.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory boundaries and buffer ownership
- Preallocated output buffers and bounds safety
- Error code to Go error mapping
- Concurrency of CGO calls and buffering

## Code Example
